        <section id="work" data-screen-label="Case studies" style="scroll-margin-top:76px;max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto;padding:clamp(40px,7vh,72px) clamp(18px,5vw,56px)">
          <div data-reveal="up" style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.2em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--faint)"><span style="color:var(--accent)">02</span><span style="width:26px;height:1px;background:var(--line-2)"></span><span>Case studies</span></div>
          <p data-reveal="up" data-reveal-delay="90" style="margin:var(--sp-eyebrow) 0 0;font-size:clamp(16px,1.8vw,18px);line-height:1.55;color:var(--muted);max-width:60ch">Three production systems, framed the way I think about them: problem, technical decision, result.</p>
          <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:26px;margin-top:var(--sp-block)">

            <article data-reveal="up-scale" style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;background:var(--panel);overflow:hidden">
              <div style="padding:clamp(24px,3.5vw,40px)">
                <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;align-items:baseline">
                  <div>
                    <div style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:.12em;color:var(--faint);text-transform:uppercase">Case 01 · Software Engineer · Highpoint Growth Networks</div>
                    <h3 style="font-size:clamp(24px,3.4vw,36px);font-weight:600;margin:10px 0 0;letter-spacing:-.02em">Role-based multi-agent AI with human-confirmed writes</h3>
                  </div>
                  <span style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:6px;padding:5px 9px">US · AD-TECH SAAS</span>
                </div>
                <div class="pdr-grid" style="background:var(--line);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden;margin-top:26px">
                  <div style="background:var(--bg-soft);padding:15px 18px">
                    <div style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.16em;color:var(--faint);text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:10px">Problem</div>
                    <p style="margin:0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--muted)">Four different user types — venues, advertisers, admins and internal messaging — needed AI assistance over the same production database, with radically different permissions and context. A single assistant with direct write access was not acceptable: a hallucinating model could corrupt billing records or leak data across accounts.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div style="background:var(--bg-soft);padding:15px 18px">
                    <div style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.16em;color:var(--faint);text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:10px">Technical decision</div>
                    <p style="margin:0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--ink)">A role-based multi-agent system built on OpenAI function calling, where each role exposes its own scoped toolset. The core pattern is propose/execute: the model never writes to the database — it produces a structured proposal that a human confirms before execution. For admin reporting, a scoped read-only SQL sandbox allows arbitrary queries with zero write surface.</p>
                  </div>
                  <div style="background:var(--bg-soft);padding:15px 18px">
                    <div style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:10.5px;letter-spacing:.16em;color:var(--accent);text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:10px">Result</div>
                    <p style="margin:0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.6;color:var(--ink)">AI assistants running in production against real customer data with no unauthorized writes. The propose/execute pattern became the team's default for any AI-driven feature touching persistent state.</p>
                  </div>
                </div>
